# pixi-env-task-config history

Changelog and superseded-skill archive for the merged canonical skill.

## v1.4.0 (2026-08-07)

MINOR — add the verified-local ProjectHephaestus rule for named task arguments:
inspect `pixi.toml` before appending positional paths. The `mypy` task already
defines `mypy hephaestus/ scripts/ tests/`; `pixi run mypy hephaestus/` forwards
the package path a second time and causes duplicate-module errors. The correct
command is `pixi run mypy`. CI validation remains pending.

## v1.3.0 (2026-07-18)

MINOR — record the VERIFIED HomericIntelligence pixi→uv supersession (Odysseus
ADR-018): uv is now the ecosystem-wide Python/build standard and `pixi.toml` is
removed from all HI repos. Adds a prominent supersession note near the top and a
new "uv Migration Mapping (ADR-018)" section. The key verified-ci finding
corrects a prior belief that uv "cannot" install non-Python toolchains: uv CAN
drive the full ecosystem — Mojo compiler via PyPI (`mojo==1.0.0b2`, same build id
as the conda pin, compiled real Mojo on ProjectOdyssey) and cmake/ninja/conan/
gcovr via PyPI binary wheels (C++ built green on Agamemnon 178/178, Nestor
115/115, Charybdis 15/15, Keystone 223 gtest targets); cxx-compiler/clang-tools/
openssl/libcurl-dev via apt; jq/go-yq via apt/release binaries; just via the
pinned setup-just action. Adds the task/command mapping (`pixi install` →
`uv sync --locked`; `pixi run X` → `uv run X`; `[tasks]` → justfile recipes
calling `uv run`; version-sync → `uv lock --check`), with `just` remaining the
task front door. Adds a Failed Attempts row (scoping migration to pure-Python
repos on the wrong "uv physically cannot" claim) and two verified-ci Verified-On
rows. New tags: `uv`, `adr-018`, `mojo-uv`, `migration`. Historical pixi guidance
retained intact below the note for non-HI pixi projects.

## v1.2.0 (2026-06-22)

MINOR — add the nested/recursive `pixi run` task smell (a `[tasks]` entry whose
body is itself `pixi run`), its root cause (TASKS-first resolution order), the
`depends-on` relocation fix, and the consumer-grep discipline ("the task exists"
≠ "anyone invokes it"). Captured as a PLANNING learning from ProjectHephaestus
issue #1554; observed facts are verified-local, the relocation fix is proposed
(not yet executed/CI-confirmed). Adds two planning assumption-trap rows
(issue-body file paths are approximate; a documented-gap can be present in one
sibling config and absent in another). New tags: `depends-on`,
`recursive-invocation`. New When-to-Use triggers and an Observed/Proposed
workflow subsection.

## v1.1.0 (2026-06-07)

restore core.hooksPath bootstrap failed-attempt (nuance audit pass 2)

## v1.0.0 (2026-06-07)

